# Cloudflare Pages response headers. Copied verbatim to dist/_headers by `astro build` (like public/_redirects).
# sow-158 security-prerequisite #1: a Content-Security-Policy. It is the host-level backstop the build-time
# member-markdown sanitizer cannot express (residual #2: off-host frame/connect/image beacons), plus
# clickjacking / base-uri / form-hijack hardening, plus script-XSS defense-in-depth on top of the sanitizer.
#
# ROLLOUT: shipped as Report-Only first, validated (check:csp force-enforce = 0 violations across 20 templates +
# a live Report-Only crawl: Turnstile renders, the news feed connects, YouTube embeds load, the extension bridge
# is intact), then flipped to ENFORCE on 2026-07-28. The CSP value must stay a SINGLE line (this file has no
# line-continuation). script-src/style-src carry 'unsafe-inline' for now (Stage 1); dropping it is a documented
# follow-up (Stage 2) that needs an inline-script refactor + a build-time hash generator.
#
# Cloudflare comma-JOINS a header set by two matching path rules into an intersection (most-restrictive wins), so
# a subpath can never loosen the CSP by ADDING a second rule. It CAN, however, `! ` remove the header and set a
# fresh value in the SAME rule block: the removal and the set live in two separate collections on one rule, so the
# result is the new value alone, order-independent (verified against real workerd via `wrangler pages dev`). Two
# subpaths use that, for opposite reasons:
#   - /tools/email-signature-generator/*  REMOVES the CSP outright (its vendored jzip.min.js uses eval) and keeps
#     clickjacking protection via X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN.
#   - /embed + /embed/*                   REMOVE and RESET to a policy that is TIGHTER than the global one in every
#     directive except frame-ancestors, which must admit chrome-extension: (see the rule's own comment). It sets NO
#     X-Frame-Options, deliberately: SAMEORIGIN would re-block the extension exactly as frame-ancestors 'self' did,
#     and XFO has no extension-permitting form (ALLOW-FROM is dead). Do NOT "restore consistency" with the tool rule.
# Do NOT add a global X-Frame-Options (it would comma-join to "DENY, SAMEORIGIN" on the tool subtree and break the
# tool iframe). The invariant is now: EVERY page except the /embed relay forbids CROSS-origin framing via the global
# frame-ancestors 'self', which still allows the site's own same-origin utility->tool iframes (e.g.
# /utilities/js-animate-hue/ frames /tools/...). scripts/check-headers.mjs enforces exactly that split.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' https: data:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://signup.gbti.network https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://www.youtube.com https://player.vimeo.com https://www.tiktok.com https://rumble.com https://platform.twitter.com; form-action 'self' https://signup.gbti.network; upgrade-insecure-requests

/tools/email-signature-generator/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

# The SOW-092 video relay. /embed exists ONLY to be framed by the Chrome extension: a chrome-extension:// page
# sends no HTTP Referer, YouTube rejects that (its error 153), so the extension frames this https page and this
# page frames the provider, which then sees a valid https referrer. The global frame-ancestors 'self' blocked
# exactly that ("Framing 'https://gbti.network/' violates ... frame-ancestors 'self'"), defeating the relay's whole
# purpose, so this policy admits the chrome-extension: SCHEME. Note a blanket `*` would NOT work: it matches only
# network schemes (http/https/ws/wss), so the scheme has to be named. The scheme source rather than a pinned
# chrome-extension://<id> because an UNPACKED dev build's id is path-derived and differs per checkout, so a pin
# breaks every developer load. Safe to loosen HERE and nowhere else: the page is session-less and form-less, and
# ?u= only ever reaches iframe.src after passing the shared embedUrl() extractor, so no attacker-controlled text
# reaches the DOM. Everything else is TIGHTER than the global policy (no Turnstile, no connect-src, no images, no
# fonts) because the relay needs none of it. TWO rules: astro trailingSlash is 'ignore', so /embed serves the same
# page and an /embed/* rule alone would miss it; /embed* is wrong (it would splat onto a future /embedded-*).
/embed
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; frame-src https://www.youtube.com https://player.vimeo.com https://www.tiktok.com https://rumble.com; frame-ancestors 'self' chrome-extension:; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'none'

/embed/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; frame-src https://www.youtube.com https://player.vimeo.com https://www.tiktok.com https://rumble.com; frame-ancestors 'self' chrome-extension:; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'none'
